From: OpenWrt mt76 PR #1166 (viewer-dental)
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7603: defer watchdog work after channel failure

On mt7603_set_channel() failure, the mt76 core already holds the
device mutex. Calling mt7603_mac_work() synchronously recursively takes
that mutex and can deadlock the entire wireless control path.
Queue delayed work instead, after the channel callback returns and the
core releases its mutex.

Upstream: https://github.com/openwrt/mt76/pull/1166
Upstream status at preparation: pending review, not merged.
Target mt76 source commit: 39c960c3ada558b4c2e7915772483d3731573d09
This fixes the error-path deadlock; it does not fix the original
cause of beacon loss. Requires full image rebuild and hardware UAT.
Never install as a mismatched .ko on a running router.

--- a/mt7603/main.c
+++ b/mt7603/main.c
@@ -193,7 +193,8 @@ int mt7603_set_channel(struct mt76_phy *mphy)
 	tasklet_enable(&dev->mt76.pre_tbtt_tasklet);
 
 	if (failed)
-		mt7603_mac_work(&dev->mphy.mac_work.work);
+		ieee80211_queue_delayed_work(mt76_hw(dev),
+					     &dev->mphy.mac_work, 0);
 
 	return ret;
 }
